Unit, run against skeleton exports: `npx tsx --test --test-reporter=spec tests/unit/routes.test.ts tests/unit/steps.test.ts` gave 25 tests, 18 failed. Seven passed: six routes tests that pin unchanged URLs, and one steps test that passes vacuously on an empty row list. Key failures:
- the `/assignment` path parsed to `null` instead of `tab: 'assignment'`;
- `assignmentPathname` built `…/run-1` without `/assignment`;
- `stepRows` returned `[]`;
- `timeAxis` returned -1 where 0 was expected.

Triage fix, test first: `tests/unit/triage.test.ts` gave 61 tests, 1 failed. The reason read "coverage was superseded (no verdict). general blocked …" instead of starting with "general blocked".

Outcome rule, test first: `tests/unit/steps.test.ts` gave 17 tests, 1 failed. The outcome showed the old gate failure instead of "repair 1: snapshot …".

Browser, worker phase: `npx playwright test -c tests/project-workflows/playwright.config.ts ux-run.spec.ts` failed all 6 scenarios.
- run-now-banner, run-steps-timeline, narrow-run and question-attention: `run-now` not found.
- graph-fits: the graph box scrolled sideways at 1280 px (scrollWidth 1688 > 1212).
- assignment-routed: the URL stayed `…/run-succeeded` instead of ending in `/assignment`.

Browser, candidate phase (`WORKFLOW_VERIFICATION_PHASE=candidate`): the same 6 failures with the same messages.

Three test-authoring mistakes were fixed and recorded separately from product reds:
- the legend assertion used `toHaveText`, but the list items also hold visually hidden text;
- two banner assignments were unused;
- the steps test expected a 2m17s span where the real one is 2m16s.
